{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And you shall make an altar for burning incense.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: The incense altar was among the inner vessels, and it is fitting to mention it together with the table and the menorah, since it is placed among them, as he mentioned so in the section of ויקהל. And the reason it is mentioned here, after the Tabernacle and all its vessels and the sacrifices, is because after it said in the completion of all — ״ונקדש בכבודי״ and ״ושכנתי בתוך בני ישראל״ — He said that they are further obligated to make an altar for burning incense, to burn incense for the glory of the Holy One, blessed be He. And this is what was transmitted to Moses, that the incense stays the plague, for the incense is the attribute of judgment, as is said (Deuteronomy 33:10): ״ישימו קטורה באפך״, from ״וחרה אפי״; and this is what He said concerning the incense of a stranger (Leviticus 10:3): ״ועל פני כל העם אכבד״ — I will be honored before all the people — that they may know My honor, for He does not forgive their transgression, and they will be careful with My honor — end quote. And since the Rav has explained for us here the matter of the incense in its secret, henceforth it is fitting for every discerning person to reject the view of the Rambam, who wrote concerning this in his reasons for the commandments: Since the Tent of Meeting was a place where the portions of the sacrifices were cut up and the entrails were washed, therefore He commanded to burn incense in that place, in order to remove and dispel that odor, and so that the good fragrance would prevail and rise in that place, and also upon the garments of the attendants there." "<b>And behold,</b> the Rav was compelled to say thus, following the path he pursued in the other commandments. But heaven forbid that the great principle within the secret of the incense — for which the Torah imposed the penalty of excision (karet) upon one who compounds it like its formula — should be dependent on this weak reason. And in the matter of Nadav and Avihu, I shall explain to you the secret of the incense, if Elohim be with me."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:05:35.021620780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}